  "query_preview": "..\n\nAn upper level jet streak will eject through the basal \nsubgeostrophic portion of Eastern North America troughing today \ncausing significant filling of geopotential heights over the central \nGreat Lakes for the end of the week. Low to midlevel temperatures \nwill steadily moderate over the coming days with 850mb temperatures \nnow at +7C to +8C rising +12C to +13C by Friday evening. High \ntemperatures today are expected to be in the upper 70s with low to \nmiddle 80s by Saturday. Strong upper level low pressure system over \nHudson Bay will help facilitate well organized northwest flow and \ntroughing over the Great by late Saturday and Sunday. \n\nModels have been adamant in forecasting an abundance of shortwave \nenergy digging through Lower Michigan in northwest flow the latter \nhalf of the weekend and into the beginning of next week. From this \nvantage point, precipitation chances appear to be scattered during \nthe late weekend period with the strongest synoptic support for low \npressure arriving sometime late Monday or Tuesday. Conditions \nproject to be very warm and humid Sunday through Tuesday with \ntemperatures in the upper 80s to lower 90s and dewpoints in the 60s \nto low 70s.",
